<p>In this example, repairing first edges out the credit, and both beat the cash offer. If repairs ran higher, or the house needed other major work, the cash sale could come out ahead. Run your own numbers with the <a href="/tools/seller-net-proceeds-calculator/">seller net proceeds calculator</a>. Before signing a repair amendment or an as-is contract, have a Texas real estate attorney or your agent review the terms.</p>
